1482
00:58:06,750 --> 00:58:07,750
-TOM: Oh.
-It's horrible.

1483
00:58:07,750 --> 00:58:08,750
TOM: Oh, just go out
and get yourself a new pair

1484
00:58:08,750 --> 00:58:10,750
of disco camping boots
there, dear.

1485
00:58:10,750 --> 00:58:11,750
MOLLY: Warm up the Jeep.

1486
00:58:12,250 --> 00:58:14,760
Molly, the road is
in a terrible condition.

1487
00:58:14,750 --> 00:58:15,250
Come on, Bill.

1488
00:58:15,250 --> 00:58:16,750
If anyone can get through,
you can.

1489
00:58:16,760 --> 00:58:17,760
We've got to try.

1490
00:58:18,260 --> 00:58:19,760
Listen, I'll come with you.
I'll just get...

1491
00:58:19,760 --> 00:58:22,260
No, I'll go.
You stay with Sharon.

1492
00:58:22,260 --> 00:58:23,770
Why don't we all go
in the camper?

1493
00:58:23,760 --> 00:58:26,260
-JOEL: Oh, just go! Somebody.
-TOM: Come on.

1494
00:58:26,270 --> 00:58:27,270
MOLLY: What about the phone,
then?

1495
00:58:27,270 --> 00:58:29,270
Lines are still down.
I just tried it.

1496
00:58:29,770 --> 00:58:30,770
Well, that's it.

1497
00:58:30,770 --> 00:58:32,270
What are we gonna do?
Find the rangers?

1498
00:58:33,270 --> 00:58:35,280
CROW:
Pepperidge Farm remembers.

1499
00:58:35,270 --> 00:58:36,270
[ Thunder rumbling ]

1500
00:58:37,780 --> 00:58:40,280
TOM: Mm, mm, mm, mm.

1501
00:58:40,280 --> 00:58:41,780
You're a good kid.

1502
00:58:42,280 --> 00:58:43,790
JOEL: Remind me
to use you later.

1503
00:58:44,780 --> 00:58:46,280
CROW: Hope she doesn't miss

1504
00:58:46,290 --> 00:58:47,790
her Josie and the Pussycats
audition.

1505
00:58:48,790 --> 00:58:50,290
[ Engine starting ]

1506
00:58:51,290 --> 00:58:52,790
JOEL: You know,
I never liked him.

1507
00:58:52,790 --> 00:58:53,800
TOM: Aloha.

1508
00:58:54,790 --> 00:58:55,790
Auf wiedersehen.

1509
00:58:56,300 --> 00:58:58,800
[ Thunder rumbling ]

1510
00:59:09,310 --> 00:59:10,310
TOM: Mm-hm.

1511
00:59:11,310 --> 00:59:15,320
Okay, you've drawn Siegfried.
Now, where's Roy?

1512
00:59:16,820 --> 00:59:17,820
TOMMY: That's my mommy.

1513
00:59:17,820 --> 00:59:18,820
-CROW: Aah!
-TOM: Ooh.

1514
00:59:18,820 --> 00:59:19,820
TOMMY: Do you have a mommy?

1515
00:59:19,820 --> 00:59:22,320
CROW: He was born of an omelet.
Of course not.

1516
00:59:22,320 --> 00:59:22,820
TOMMY: You don't know?

1517
00:59:29,330 --> 00:59:30,330
TOMMY: Does she look like this?

1518
00:59:30,330 --> 00:59:31,830
-CROW: Ooh.
-TOM: No, no.

1519
00:59:32,330 --> 00:59:33,330
TOMMY: Or like this?

1520
00:59:33,330 --> 00:59:34,840
TOM: Any distinguishing marks
or scars?

1521
00:59:34,830 --> 00:59:35,330
Where is she, then?

1522
00:59:36,340 --> 00:59:37,840
CROW: Where did he learn
English?

1523
00:59:37,840 --> 00:59:39,340
TOMMY: Oh, she's in a tree.

1524
00:59:39,840 --> 00:59:42,340
JOEL: Uh, I can tell by
the expression on your face

1525
00:59:42,340 --> 00:59:45,850
that you loved her so, Trumpy.

1526
00:59:46,350 --> 00:59:48,350
TOM: What,
she's from Rand McNally?

1527
00:59:49,350 --> 00:59:50,850
TOMMY: On a star?

1528
00:59:50,850 --> 00:59:53,350
CROW: Can she carry moonbeams
home in a jar?

1529
00:59:53,350 --> 00:59:54,860
TOMMY: Wow!

1530
00:59:54,850 --> 00:59:56,350
With this you can see
the stars.

1531
00:59:56,860 --> 00:59:57,860
You want to look?

1532
00:59:58,360 --> 00:59:59,860
TOM: This kid sounds
like Georgette.

1533
00:59:59,860 --> 01:00:00,860
JOEL: Yeah.

1534
01:00:03,860 --> 01:00:04,860
CROW: Kitty.

1535
01:00:04,860 --> 01:00:07,360
JOEL: Oh, they got "Wild
Kingdom" on that telescope.

1536
01:00:07,870 --> 01:00:09,370
TOM: Cool.

1537
01:00:10,870 --> 01:00:12,870
[ Drums beating ]

1538
01:00:15,870 --> 01:00:17,370
JOEL: Mm-hm.

1539
01:00:18,880 --> 01:00:20,380
And drums, too?

1540
01:00:20,380 --> 01:00:21,880
TOMMY: You can do magic things.

1541
01:00:22,380 --> 01:00:24,390
CROW: It's called evil, kid.

1542
01:00:24,380 --> 01:00:25,380
TOM: He's got his high beams on.

1543
01:00:25,880 --> 01:00:26,880
Hmm?

1544
01:00:28,390 --> 01:00:30,390
JOEL: He's got Bette Davis eyes.

1545
01:00:30,390 --> 01:00:31,390
[ Tom laughs ]

1546
01:00:31,890 --> 01:00:32,890
CROW: Orphan Annie eyes.

1547
01:00:34,390 --> 01:00:35,890
JOEL: Oh, great,
now we're in "Gumby".

1548
01:00:35,890 --> 01:00:36,390
TOM: Whoo!

1549
01:00:37,400 --> 01:00:39,900
CROW: I'm going to go walk
through a book.

1550
01:00:40,900 --> 01:00:41,400
TOM: Ooh, it's

1551
01:00:41,400 --> 01:00:43,400
supercalafragilistic-
expialidocious.

1552
01:00:43,400 --> 01:00:45,410
[ Tom giggles ]
D'oh.

1553
01:00:45,400 --> 01:00:46,900
CROW: I love this.
It's so spontaneous.

1554
01:00:46,910 --> 01:00:48,910
-TOM: Whoo!
-[ Crow laughs ]

1555
01:00:49,910 --> 01:00:52,410
JOEL: Oh, wow, we're in
"Pee-Wee's Playhouse" now.

1556
01:00:52,410 --> 01:00:53,920
CROW: Oh, yuck.

1557
01:00:55,910 --> 01:00:57,910
CROW: It's a Peter Gabriel
video.

1558
01:00:58,420 --> 01:00:59,420
TOM: Yeah, somebody hit that kid
in the head with a...

1559
01:00:59,420 --> 01:01:00,920
sledge hammer.

1560
01:01:00,920 --> 01:01:02,420
[ Laughing ]

1561
01:01:03,920 --> 01:01:07,920
JOEL: Wow. Oh, this alien
makes student films, huh?

1562
01:01:07,930 --> 01:01:09,930
TOM: What, did he come
from Planet Goofball?

1563
01:01:10,430 --> 01:01:12,430
Did he come here
in a little clown car?

1564
01:01:12,930 --> 01:01:13,940
Criminy.

1565
01:01:13,930 --> 01:01:16,430
JOEL: Great, now he can remake
"Rudolph's Shiny New Year."

1566
01:01:16,440 --> 01:01:17,440
[ Tom chuckling ]

1567
01:01:17,940 --> 01:01:18,940
TOM: Poor rabbit.

1568
01:01:19,940 --> 01:01:20,940
CROW: Poor us.

1569
01:01:20,940 --> 01:01:22,940
TOMMY: Trumpy?
Where are you?

1570
01:01:23,440 --> 01:01:25,950
CROW: Get me!
I'm Lionel Richie!

1571
01:01:25,940 --> 01:01:26,940
JOEL: That's not right.

1572
01:01:26,950 --> 01:01:28,450
TOMMY: Trumpy.

1573
01:01:28,950 --> 01:01:29,450
TOM: Huh?

1574
01:01:29,950 --> 01:01:31,450
TOMMY: Hey, come back down.

1575
01:01:31,450 --> 01:01:33,450
TOM: Really looked
like a ceiling. Didn't it?

1576
01:01:37,460 --> 01:01:38,960
Oh, fun.

1577
01:01:38,960 --> 01:01:39,460
CROW: Whew!

1578
01:01:40,460 --> 01:01:41,460
MOLLY: Tommy,
what are you doing?

1579
01:01:41,460 --> 01:01:44,970
JOEL: It's just my Spike Jones
album, Mom!

1580
01:01:45,460 --> 01:01:46,460
TOM: Tommy, now,

1581
01:01:46,470 --> 01:01:48,970
you quit warping time and space
this instant.

1582
01:01:49,470 --> 01:01:52,970
MOLLY: Tommy.
Did you hear me, Tommy?

1583
01:01:53,470 --> 01:01:54,980
-Come on, quickly.
-CROW: Busted.

1584
01:01:54,970 --> 01:01:55,970
Hide in there.

1585
01:01:56,480 --> 01:01:57,480
[ Imitating Trumpy ]

1586
01:02:00,480 --> 01:02:01,480
Are you okay?

1587
01:02:01,480 --> 01:02:02,480
TOMMY: Yes, Mom.

1588
01:02:03,480 --> 01:02:04,490
What's going on here?

1589
01:02:04,480 --> 01:02:05,980
-Little Joe got out.
-What?

1590
01:02:05,980 --> 01:02:06,980
My hamster Joe escaped.

1591
01:02:06,990 --> 01:02:08,990
Well, try and be a little more
careful.

1592
01:02:08,990 --> 01:02:09,990
I told you a thousand times,
I don't want you...

1593
01:02:09,990 --> 01:02:10,990
TOM: I'd like some
breakfast please.

1594
01:02:10,990 --> 01:02:11,490
...turning this house
into a zoo.

1595
01:02:12,490 --> 01:02:14,000
And stop fidgeting around
like that.

1596
01:02:13,990 --> 01:02:14,990
Yes, Mommy.

1597
01:02:14,990 --> 01:02:17,490
All right. Now, come downstairs
with me and behave yourself.

1598
01:02:17,500 --> 01:02:19,770
I've got enough problems.

1599
01:02:21,530 --> 01:02:23,030
TOM: Make that three
hard-boiled eggs.

1600
01:02:23,040 --> 01:02:24,540
CROW: I've got to get a series.

1601
01:02:28,040 --> 01:02:30,550
JOEL: Now, do you think
those are blue contacts,

1602
01:02:30,540 --> 01:02:32,540
or are his eyes naturally
that color?

1603
01:02:32,540 --> 01:02:34,540
TOM: Oh, you mean,
like Whoopi Goldberg?

1604
01:02:34,550 --> 01:02:35,050
JOEL: Yeah.

1605
01:02:35,050 --> 01:02:36,050
[ Tom laughs ]

1606
01:02:39,050 --> 01:02:42,060
TOM: Get my head caught
in the snout there.

1607
01:02:42,050 --> 01:02:45,550
CROW: Now to find a herd
of cattle to drain dry.

1608
01:02:47,060 --> 01:02:49,830
TOM: Meanwhile in a winter movie
somewhere.

1609
01:02:49,830 --> 01:02:52,330
JOEL: Gosh, that last scene
was goofy.

1610
01:02:52,330 --> 01:02:53,840
I'm glad we weren't in it.

1611
01:02:54,330 --> 01:02:56,330
BILL: Ah, sometimes there is.

1612
01:02:56,340 --> 01:02:58,340
I thought hunting
wasn't allowed around here.

1613
01:02:58,340 --> 01:02:59,340
It's not.

1614
01:02:59,340 --> 01:03:00,840
Why are you carrying this rifle,
then?

1615
01:03:00,840 --> 01:03:01,840
TOM: For you.

1616
01:03:01,840 --> 01:03:03,850
Well, if that friend of yours
Laura had carried one,

1617
01:03:04,840 --> 01:03:06,340
she'd still be alive.

1618
01:03:06,350 --> 01:03:07,350
JOEL: Hurts.

1619
01:03:07,350 --> 01:03:08,350
TOM: Ooh.

1620
01:03:08,350 --> 01:03:11,850
CROW: Hey, it's a matching shirt
and sofa set.

1621
01:03:13,350 --> 01:03:14,360
TOM: Hi, gang.

1622
01:03:14,350 --> 01:03:15,350
[ Tom humming ]

1623
01:03:15,850 --> 01:03:17,350
TOM: Hmm, not bad.

1624
01:03:18,860 --> 01:03:20,860
Oh, the new Vogue is here.

1625
01:03:22,360 --> 01:03:23,870
TRACY: Molly,
is the television working?

1626
01:03:23,860 --> 01:03:25,360
I think so, yes.

1627
01:03:25,360 --> 01:03:27,360
Well, at least we won't miss
"Dallas" this week.

1628
01:03:27,870 --> 01:03:29,370
CROW: Oh great,
your friend just died,

1629
01:03:29,370 --> 01:03:30,370
and you're gonna watch "Dallas"?

1630
01:03:30,870 --> 01:03:31,370
TOM: Tsst.

1631
01:03:32,870 --> 01:03:34,880
KATHY: Tracy, how can you kid
around like this,

1632
01:03:34,870 --> 01:03:36,370
things being the way they are?

1633
01:03:36,880 --> 01:03:37,880
TOM: Thank you.

1634
01:03:37,880 --> 01:03:40,380
TRACY: Because if I didn't,
I'd be in hysterics.

1635
01:03:40,380 --> 01:03:42,380
-It doesn't work.
-JOEL: I'm in hysterics!

1636
01:03:42,380 --> 01:03:43,380
That's strange.

1637
01:03:43,380 --> 01:03:44,890
It was working yesterday.

1638
01:03:45,380 --> 01:03:46,880
JOEL: I rerouted the power
into Trumpy.

1639
01:03:46,890 --> 01:03:48,390
The radio makes
a funny noise, too.

1640
01:03:48,390 --> 01:03:49,890
TOM: Uh, that's called music.

1641
01:03:49,890 --> 01:03:51,390
TOMMY: Can I go back to my room,
Mommy?

1642
01:03:51,390 --> 01:03:52,390
Yes, you can.

1643
01:03:52,390 --> 01:03:54,400
CROW: For the rest of your life.

1644
01:03:58,400 --> 01:03:59,400
KATHY: How is Sharon?

1645
01:03:59,900 --> 01:04:01,400
She's gone to bed.
She was shattered.

1646
01:04:01,900 --> 01:04:04,410
-JOEL: This town's in tatters.
-TOM: Shadoobie.

1647
01:04:04,400 --> 01:04:06,900
TRACY: So peaceful, so quiet.
[ Tracy chuckles ]

1648
01:04:07,410 --> 01:04:08,910
[ Tom chuckles like Tracy ]

1649
01:04:13,410 --> 01:04:14,920
TOMMY: Trumpy.

1650
01:04:16,420 --> 01:04:18,420
[ Joel makes snarling noise ]

1651
01:04:18,420 --> 01:04:18,920
[ Tom chuckles ]

1652
01:04:19,920 --> 01:04:22,920
TOM: Face it, kid.
Trumpy never loved you.

1653
01:04:25,420 --> 01:04:26,420
Boo! Gotcha!

1654
01:04:26,430 --> 01:04:27,430
[ Tom laughs ]

1655
01:04:27,430 --> 01:04:28,430
TOMMY: Trumpy, where are you?

1656
01:04:28,930 --> 01:04:31,930
JOEL: Were ties ever that wide?

1657
01:04:34,430 --> 01:04:36,430
-Ah.
-TOM: Ah.

1658
01:04:38,940 --> 01:04:40,940
CROW: All right.
S'all right.

1659
01:04:42,440 --> 01:04:42,940
JOEL: Nothin'

1660
01:04:43,940 --> 01:04:44,940
CROW: Hmm.

1661
01:04:47,450 --> 01:04:48,450
[ Cat meows ]

1662
01:04:48,450 --> 01:04:49,450
TOMMY: Have you seen Trumpy?

1663
01:04:49,950 --> 01:04:52,450
JOEL: He tried to eat me.
He's evil.

1664
01:04:52,450 --> 01:04:54,460
TOM: Forget you.

1665
01:04:55,450 --> 01:04:55,950
Boo!

1666
01:04:55,950 --> 01:04:56,950
[ Tom laughs ]

1667
01:05:06,300 --> 01:05:08,300
-TOM: Cujo?
-JOEL: Evil one?

1668
01:05:09,300 --> 01:05:11,310
-JOEL: Supreme being?
-CROW: Alf?

1669
01:05:11,300 --> 01:05:14,300
-TOM: Chief?
-CROW: McCloud?

1670
01:05:14,810 --> 01:05:19,310
TOMMY: Trumpy, come on.
Where are you?

1671
01:05:21,810 --> 01:05:23,310
CROW: He seeks him here.

1672
01:05:23,320 --> 01:05:24,320
He seeks him there.

1673
01:05:24,320 --> 01:05:27,320
He seeks that rascal
everywhere.

1674
01:05:28,320 --> 01:05:31,830
TOM: Ah, don't worry about him.
He's moody and introspective.

1675
01:05:31,820 --> 01:05:33,820
He's in a corner reading
"Swimming to Cambodia".

1676
01:05:34,830 --> 01:05:35,830
CROW: Hmm.

1677
01:05:35,830 --> 01:05:38,330
TOMMY: Trumpy, are you in here?

1678
01:05:38,330 --> 01:05:41,840
JOEL: This is, like, the house
of a million foyers.

1679
01:05:41,830 --> 01:05:43,830
[ Suspenseful ]
TOM: Dum, dum

1680
01:05:44,340 --> 01:05:46,340
CROW: Dad?

1681
01:05:46,340 --> 01:05:47,340
TOM: Dum

1682
01:05:47,840 --> 01:05:49,840
-CROW: Dad?
-TOM: Dum

1683
01:05:52,840 --> 01:05:55,340
TOM: Don't go
into the dining room.

1684
01:05:57,850 --> 01:05:59,850
JOEL: Here's Tommy!

1685
01:05:59,850 --> 01:06:01,360
TOMMY: Trumpy.

1686
01:06:04,860 --> 01:06:05,860
JOEL: Sounds like music

1687
01:06:05,860 --> 01:06:07,860
from the "High Plains Drifter",
doesn't it?

1688
01:06:07,860 --> 01:06:09,360
-TOM: Mm-hm.
-CROW: Yeah.

1689
01:06:09,860 --> 01:06:12,870
TOM: Has a Sergio Leone
feel to it.

1690
01:06:14,870 --> 01:06:15,870
CROW: Bad choice.

1691
01:06:15,870 --> 01:06:17,870
JOEL: Oh, those are ready
to pop, I would say.

1692
01:06:21,870 --> 01:06:22,870
[ Imitating grinding noise ]

1693
01:06:23,380 --> 01:06:25,880
TOM: Oh, thank goodness
it's summer again.

1694
01:06:26,380 --> 01:06:28,880
We've been driving for months.

1695
01:06:30,380 --> 01:06:32,390
BILL: Doesn't look
like anybody's in.

1696
01:06:32,880 --> 01:06:35,380
But how can you tell
from here?

1697
01:06:35,390 --> 01:06:38,390
TOM: Oh, why don't you just go
up to the door?

1698
01:06:38,390 --> 01:06:39,890
You drove two seasons
to get here.

1699
01:06:41,390 --> 01:06:42,890
For crying out loud.

1700
01:06:42,890 --> 01:06:44,890
CROW: Boy,
he's really burning oil.

1701
01:06:44,900 --> 01:06:46,400
TOM: Mm-hm.

1702
01:06:47,900 --> 01:06:50,400
JOEL: I'm going to let this
do the talking.

1703
01:06:51,900 --> 01:06:55,400
BILL: Charley? Jack?
Is anyone there?

1704
01:06:55,410 --> 01:06:57,410
JOEL: He knows them,
and he's bringing a gun?

1705
01:06:57,410 --> 01:06:58,410
TOM: Oh,
it's a little practical joke.

1706
01:06:58,410 --> 01:07:00,920
He kicks open the door
and plugs them with 30 rounds.

1707
01:07:00,910 --> 01:07:02,910
It's kind of an inside family
thing, you know.

1708
01:07:02,910 --> 01:07:03,910
CROW: Housewarming gift.

1709
01:07:03,920 --> 01:07:05,420
TOM: Mm-hm.

1710
01:07:08,420 --> 01:07:09,420
-JOEL: Aah!
-TOM: Ooh.

1711
01:07:09,420 --> 01:07:10,420
JOEL: Oh, it's that guy.

1712
01:07:10,420 --> 01:07:11,930
-What do you think you're...?
-Shh.

1713
01:07:11,920 --> 01:07:13,920
JOEL: Hey, Bill, are those
Haggar slacks you're wearing?

1714
01:07:14,430 --> 01:07:15,930
Farah?
Dad N' Lad?

1715
01:07:16,430 --> 01:07:17,930
The Guys?

1716
01:07:17,930 --> 01:07:18,930
[ Tom chuckling ]

1717
01:07:18,930 --> 01:07:21,440
CROW: Watch this.
Little joke.

1718
01:07:21,930 --> 01:07:23,930
CROW: Hi! We're the cast
from "Straw Dogs".

1719
01:07:23,940 --> 01:07:25,940
[ Crow laughing uneasily ]

1720
01:07:28,440 --> 01:07:29,940
TOM: Sometimes it works.

1721
01:07:32,440 --> 01:07:33,940
TOM: Watchtower!
Oh, just kidding.

1722
01:07:33,950 --> 01:07:34,950
[ Tom & Crow chuckle ]

1723
01:07:34,950 --> 01:07:36,450
TOM: That thing in the magazine.

1724
01:07:36,450 --> 01:07:38,450
BRIAN: What the hell
happened here?

1725
01:07:39,450 --> 01:07:40,960
TOM: Hmm.

1726
01:07:41,950 --> 01:07:43,450
JOEL: Hmm.

1727
01:07:43,960 --> 01:07:44,960
BILL: The radio's not working.

1728
01:07:44,960 --> 01:07:46,960
CROW: Oh, nuts! I wanted
to hear Shadoe Stevens.

1729
01:07:46,960 --> 01:07:47,960
BILL: Charley? Jack?

1730
01:07:47,960 --> 01:07:50,460
JOEL: Biff? Happy? Anybody?

1731
01:07:50,960 --> 01:07:52,460
BRIAN: You think they're
in the other roo...

1732
01:07:52,960 --> 01:07:55,460
After all this shouting,
I sure hope not.

1733
01:07:55,970 --> 01:08:00,470
JOEL: Horse poster compliments
Dynamite magazine. For teens.

1734
01:08:04,480 --> 01:08:05,480
CROW: Turkey legs in the...

1735
01:08:05,980 --> 01:08:06,480
[ Groans ]

1736
01:08:07,980 --> 01:08:08,980
BRIAN: He's dead, I think.

1737
01:08:10,480 --> 01:08:12,490
TOM: His last words were,
"Huzzah!"

1738
01:08:12,480 --> 01:08:13,480
BILL: What's that?

1739
01:08:14,990 --> 01:08:16,990
Same mark that... Laura had.

1740
01:08:17,990 --> 01:08:18,990
Is he one of the rangers?

1741
01:08:19,490 --> 01:08:21,500
JOEL: No, but we could dress him
like a ranger.

1742
01:08:21,490 --> 01:08:23,490
BILL: No, he's a poacher,
name of Matt Collins.

1743
01:08:26,500 --> 01:08:28,500
Let's get the hell
out of here.

1744
01:08:30,500 --> 01:08:31,510
I don't know.

1745
01:08:31,500 --> 01:08:32,500
[ Growling ]

1746
01:08:32,500 --> 01:08:33,500
BILL: Look out! Jesus!

1747
01:08:33,510 --> 01:08:34,510
CROW: Aah!

1748
01:08:35,510 --> 01:08:38,010
CROW: Alf's back,
and this time it's personal.

1749
01:08:38,010 --> 01:08:39,010
[ Tom chuckling ]

1750
01:08:41,510 --> 01:08:43,010
TOM: Ooh, Reagan's next.

1751
01:08:43,520 --> 01:08:45,520
CROW: Pepperidge Farm remembers!
Pepperidge Farm remembers!

1752
01:08:46,020 --> 01:08:47,520
The heck with it.
I'm getting out of here!

1753
01:08:48,020 --> 01:08:49,020
Crackers or no!

1754
01:08:51,520 --> 01:08:54,020
TOM: That is the frumpiest...
monster I've ever seen.

1755
01:08:54,030 --> 01:08:55,030
JOEL: Yep.

1756
01:08:57,530 --> 01:08:59,530
CROW: Hey, wait!
You got coupons comin'.

1757
01:09:00,030 --> 01:09:02,540
JOEL: No hitchhikers.
It's company policy.

1758
01:09:02,530 --> 01:09:03,530
TOM: Ooh.

1759
01:09:03,540 --> 01:09:05,040
Ah, enough
of that exciting stuff.

1760
01:09:05,040 --> 01:09:07,540
Meanwhile, in still yet
another movie.

1761
01:09:08,040 --> 01:09:09,040
[ Sighs ]

1762
01:09:13,040 --> 01:09:15,040
[ Tom hiccups ]

1763
01:09:16,050 --> 01:09:16,550
CROW: What the...?

1764
01:09:17,550 --> 01:09:19,050
MOLLY: You're a good cook,
Tracy.

1765
01:09:19,050 --> 01:09:20,550
Unusual with girls today.

1766
01:09:20,550 --> 01:09:21,560
Well, my mother taught me.

1767
01:09:22,050 --> 01:09:24,050
She always said that men
like you for your meat

1768
01:09:24,060 --> 01:09:25,560
and after, your dessert.
[ Tom groans ]

1769
01:09:25,560 --> 01:09:26,560
You know how it is.

1770
01:09:26,560 --> 01:09:28,560
If you haven't got a pretty face
to begin with,

1771
01:09:28,560 --> 01:09:30,060
there's nothing you can do.

1772
01:09:30,060 --> 01:09:32,570
JOEL: Well, I think your mother
had a filthy mouth.

1773
01:09:32,560 --> 01:09:35,060
TRACY:...including
the 7-day beauty plan.

1774
01:09:35,070 --> 01:09:36,070
TOM: Didn't work.

1775
01:09:36,570 --> 01:09:38,070
MOLLY: Come on.
It's not that bad.

1776
01:09:38,070 --> 01:09:39,070
You've got a lot
of good points.

1777
01:09:39,570 --> 01:09:41,580
Yeah, and I know
the ones men like.

1778
01:09:41,570 --> 01:09:43,070
These and this.

1779
01:09:43,070 --> 01:09:44,070
But you're very intelligent.

1780
01:09:44,080 --> 01:09:46,080
Yeah, I don't know what
threatens the guys more...

1781
01:09:46,080 --> 01:09:47,080
my face or my intelligence.

1782
01:09:47,080 --> 01:09:50,580
CROW: Yeah, E=mc2.

1783
01:09:52,580 --> 01:09:54,580
TRACY: Hey, I'm getting a bit
worried about Brian and Bill.

1784
01:09:55,090 --> 01:09:56,090
They've been gone now
for hours.

1785
01:09:56,090 --> 01:09:57,590
Oh, maybe they got held up.

1786
01:09:58,090 --> 01:09:59,590
Or couldn't find the rangers.

1787
01:09:59,590 --> 01:10:01,600
Oh, yeah, these rangers.

1788
01:10:01,590 --> 01:10:03,590
JOEL: Down, girl.
Heel. Take it easy.

1789
01:10:03,600 --> 01:10:05,100
TRACY: All right, Molly.
I know.

1790
01:10:05,600 --> 01:10:06,600
Just in case, however,

1791
01:10:06,600 --> 01:10:08,100
I'm going to get my makeup
from the camper.

1792
01:10:08,100 --> 01:10:09,600
-I forgot it last night.
-TOM: Take a cold shower.

1793
01:10:10,100 --> 01:10:11,610
Now, what's going on, Tommy?

1794
01:10:11,600 --> 01:10:12,600
You've been running
in and out all day.

1795
01:10:13,100 --> 01:10:13,600
What are you looking for?

1796
01:10:14,610 --> 01:10:16,610
Nothing. Just getting
some water for Joe.

1797
01:10:16,610 --> 01:10:17,610
-Oh.
-Joe?

1798
01:10:18,610 --> 01:10:20,610
Are you hiding a man somewhere
in this house?

1799
01:10:20,610 --> 01:10:22,620
Joe is Tommy's hamster, Tracy.

1800
01:10:22,610 --> 01:10:24,610
-Oh, what a shame.
-TOM: Geez, Tracy, stay away

1801
01:10:24,620 --> 01:10:26,120
from the kid's animals.

1802
01:10:27,620 --> 01:10:28,620
[ Thunder rumbling ]

1803
01:10:31,620 --> 01:10:32,620
[ Tom humming ]

1804
01:10:33,120 --> 01:10:34,120
[ Crow whistles ]

1805
01:10:34,130 --> 01:10:37,630
CROW: Ba-dump-a-dee
Time to Armor All my pants.

1806
01:10:40,630 --> 01:10:41,640
JOEL: Oh, this is great.

1807
01:10:41,630 --> 01:10:43,630
He's gonna do
that Bob Newhart routine.

1808
01:10:43,640 --> 01:10:44,640
-[ Tom chuckles ]
-TOM: Love that.

1809
01:10:45,140 --> 01:10:47,140
JOEL: Uh, Abner? Yeah, hello.

1810
01:10:51,140 --> 01:10:52,140
Still isn't working.

1811
01:10:53,140 --> 01:10:54,640
Where the hell have Brian
and that old geezer got to?

1812
01:10:54,650 --> 01:10:56,150
It's been seven hours
since they left.

1813
01:10:56,650 --> 01:10:57,650
Didn't have that far to go.

1814
01:10:58,150 --> 01:10:59,150
Maybe something
happened to them.

1815
01:11:00,150 --> 01:11:01,160
Wouldn't surprise me.

1816
01:11:01,150 --> 01:11:02,150
Bill's as thick as two planks.

1817
01:11:03,150 --> 01:11:04,150
-CROW: Is he green-sheeted?
-How are Sharon and Kathy?

1818
01:11:04,660 --> 01:11:06,160
They took sleeping pills
and went to bed.

1819
01:11:06,160 --> 01:11:08,160
They were absolutely scared
out of their wits.

1820
01:11:08,160 --> 01:11:09,160
Maybe you should do the same.

1821
01:11:09,660 --> 01:11:11,670
[ Mocking ] TOM: Maybe you
should do the same.

1822
01:11:13,670 --> 01:11:16,670
[ Thunder distantly rumbles ]

1823
01:11:20,170 --> 01:11:23,680
JOEL: Trumpy? I brought you
a cup of treacle.

1824
01:11:23,680 --> 01:11:25,180
TOMMY: Trumpy.

1825
01:11:27,180 --> 01:11:28,680
-TOM: Aww.
-Where are you hiding?

1826
01:11:31,180 --> 01:11:34,680
Hey, she's got her L.L. Bean
disco survival boots on.

1827
01:11:36,190 --> 01:11:37,690
TOM: Survive in style.

1828
01:11:39,690 --> 01:11:41,200
JOEL: Trumpy, bring me the girl.

1829
01:11:41,190 --> 01:11:43,690
I desire to be read to.

1830
01:11:45,700 --> 01:11:46,700
[ Drums ]

1831
01:11:47,200 --> 01:11:49,700
TOM: Neil Peart on drums.

1832
01:11:50,200 --> 01:11:52,210
CROW: Hey, it's Craig Wasson,
all of a sudden.

1833
01:11:57,710 --> 01:12:00,710
JOEL: Now Trumpy and I will do
my version of "Rear Window".

1834
01:12:01,210 --> 01:12:02,710
[ Woman screams ]

1835
01:12:03,720 --> 01:12:05,720
TOM: I think she found Trumpy.

1836
01:12:05,720 --> 01:12:08,220
ALL: Whah, whah, whah.

1837
01:12:08,720 --> 01:12:09,220
[ Woman groans ]

1838
01:12:10,720 --> 01:12:13,230
CROW: Hey, this is not healthy
for a little boy.

1839
01:12:14,230 --> 01:12:15,230
I can't watch.

1840
01:12:15,230 --> 01:12:16,730
[ Groans continue ]

1841
01:12:18,230 --> 01:12:22,240
JOEL: Trumpy, no.
I told you no.

1842
01:12:25,240 --> 01:12:26,740
TOMMY: Trumpy.

1843
01:12:28,240 --> 01:12:31,750
TOM: When good pets do bad
things, on "A Current Affair".

1844
01:12:32,740 --> 01:12:35,740
JOEL: That was neat.

1845
01:12:36,250 --> 01:12:37,250
[ Gasps ]

1846
01:12:39,250 --> 01:12:41,760
JOEL: Trumpy, we hardly knew ye.

1847
01:12:48,760 --> 01:12:49,760
[ Tom coughs ]

1848
01:12:49,760 --> 01:12:51,270
TOM: Put out the van.

1849
01:12:56,770 --> 01:12:59,270
Oh, so people are being
methodically killed

1850
01:12:59,270 --> 01:13:01,280
by the Banana Splits.

1851
01:13:01,270 --> 01:13:02,270
JOEL: There goes Drooper.

1852
01:13:03,270 --> 01:13:05,270
-JOEL: Fleegle.
-TOM: Snork.

1853
01:13:05,780 --> 01:13:07,780
[ Gunshot ]

1854
01:13:13,790 --> 01:13:14,290
TOM: Mm-hm.

1855
01:13:15,290 --> 01:13:17,290
-Oh, my God.
-Bill.

1856
01:13:17,290 --> 01:13:19,290
-BILL: So what, she's dead?
-RICK: Yeah, she is.

1857
01:13:20,290 --> 01:13:21,300
What the hell's going on?

1858
01:13:22,290 --> 01:13:24,790
-It was a damned animal.
-What animal?

1859
01:13:24,800 --> 01:13:25,800
-CROW: The damned one.
- Where's Brian?

1860
01:13:25,800 --> 01:13:26,800
He's dead.

1861
01:13:26,800 --> 01:13:27,800
Dead? Where?

1862
01:13:28,300 --> 01:13:28,800
Back at the hut.

1863
01:13:29,800 --> 01:13:32,310
CROW: Oh, take the Baretta
hat off, old man.

1864
01:13:32,800 --> 01:13:33,800
TOM: Aww.

1865
01:13:34,810 --> 01:13:35,810
[ Tom chuckles ]

1866
01:13:35,810 --> 01:13:38,310
TOM: Faster, Trumpy, kill, kill.

1867
01:13:39,810 --> 01:13:42,320
RICK: What the hell?
What's happening?

1868
01:13:42,810 --> 01:13:44,810
Answer me, you goat.
What is this?

1869
01:13:44,820 --> 01:13:46,820
[ Tom imitates a goat ] What
have you done, you old bastard?

1870
01:13:46,820 --> 01:13:48,820
Stop it! Have you both
gone crazy?

1871
01:13:48,820 --> 01:13:52,330
I want to know who it was killed
Brian and Tracy and why.

1872
01:13:52,320 --> 01:13:53,320
-I told you.
-TOM: We have to go.

1873
01:13:53,830 --> 01:13:55,330
-JOEL: Oh.
-It was that weird animal.

1874
01:13:55,330 --> 01:13:57,830
And if we stay here,
it'll kill us all.

1875
01:13:57,830 --> 01:13:59,330
What sort of fairy tale
is this?

1876
01:13:59,330 --> 01:14:01,340
Oh, listen, Rick.
We'll sort this out later.

1877
01:14:01,330 --> 01:14:04,330
Now help Bill carry Tracy
inside.

1878
01:14:06,340 --> 01:14:07,340
Bill.

1879
01:14:22,450 --> 01:14:24,450
You are magic.
Aren't you, Trumpy?

1880
01:14:24,460 --> 01:14:25,960
[ Circus music ]

1881
01:14:41,470 --> 01:14:43,470
Trumpy, you come down.

1882
01:14:43,980 --> 01:14:45,480
[ Screaming ]

1883
01:14:45,480 --> 01:14:48,480
[ Carnival music plays ]

1884
01:15:01,990 --> 01:15:05,490
I can't bring 'em down.
I don't know how it works.

1885
01:15:11,500 --> 01:15:13,500
I'm stuck! I'm stuck!

1886
01:15:17,010 --> 01:15:20,010
Oh, we got commercial sign!

1887
01:15:20,010 --> 01:15:24,020
[ Carnival music
continues playing ]

1888
01:15:25,920 --> 01:15:27,920
I really don't know
what kind of animal it was.

1889
01:15:28,420 --> 01:15:29,920
All I know is I was very lucky.

1890
01:15:29,920 --> 01:15:32,430
Whatever it is, it's already
killed four people.

1891
01:15:32,420 --> 01:15:33,920
And maybe more.

1892
01:15:34,930 --> 01:15:35,930
Where are you going, Rick?

1893
01:15:35,930 --> 01:15:37,430
-To wake up the girls.
-Why?

1894
01:15:37,430 --> 01:15:38,430
So we can get out of here.

1895
01:15:38,430 --> 01:15:40,430
I ain't hanging about to find
out who's next for the chop.

1896
01:15:40,930 --> 01:15:42,440
-You can't leave now.
-No? Why not?

1897
01:15:42,430 --> 01:15:43,430
TOM: I made quiche.

1898
01:15:43,430 --> 01:15:45,430
BILL: It's getting dark,
'cause the road's blocked,

1899
01:15:45,440 --> 01:15:47,940
because that thing,
that murderous animal

1900
01:15:47,940 --> 01:15:48,940
is maybe waiting for us.

1901
01:15:48,940 --> 01:15:49,940
CROW: Yeah, but give me
a good reason.

1902
01:15:49,940 --> 01:15:50,940
MOLLY: He's right, you know.

1903
01:15:51,440 --> 01:15:52,940
We better wait till morning.

1904
01:15:53,440 --> 01:15:55,440
Listen, I'm sick and tired
of hearing the same old story.

1905
01:15:55,450 --> 01:15:57,450
JOEL: I'm sick and tired
of being I'm sick and tired.

1906
01:15:57,950 --> 01:15:59,450
How can you say that, Rick?

1907
01:15:59,450 --> 01:16:00,450
Well, I'm getting out of here,

1908
01:16:00,450 --> 01:16:02,460
and if I were you,
I'd take the kid and leave.

1909
01:16:02,450 --> 01:16:04,950
TOM: Kid? What kid?
Oh, my God.

1910
01:16:05,960 --> 01:16:07,960
CROW: Don't start with me,
Martha.

1911
01:16:08,460 --> 01:16:10,460
BILL: If you've got a bit
of sense, then, you'll stay.

1912
01:16:12,460 --> 01:16:14,960
He's right, Rick.
He knows the forest.

1913
01:16:16,970 --> 01:16:17,970
I'd better make sure

1914
01:16:17,970 --> 01:16:19,970
that all the doors and windows
are bolted.

1915
01:16:20,970 --> 01:16:22,480
JOEL: Now for some peach
cobbler.

1916
01:16:25,480 --> 01:16:27,480
TOM: Oh, George, get me a drink.

1917
01:16:28,980 --> 01:16:31,990
Boo? Boo Radley?

1918
01:16:31,980 --> 01:16:33,980
CROW: Dark One? Beelzebub?

1919
01:16:33,990 --> 01:16:35,490
-JOEL: Chief?
-CROW: McCloud?

1920
01:16:35,990 --> 01:16:37,490
[ Tom laughing ]

1921
01:16:38,490 --> 01:16:40,490
CROW: Trumpage! Trumpazoid!

1922
01:16:40,490 --> 01:16:41,500
The Trumpmonster!

1923
01:16:41,490 --> 01:16:42,490
TOM: Trumparino!

1924
01:16:42,990 --> 01:16:44,490
Stretching the premise.

1925
01:16:49,500 --> 01:16:50,500
[ Trumpy yelling ]

1926
01:16:50,500 --> 01:16:51,510
JOEL: He knocked his block off,

1927
01:16:51,500 --> 01:16:52,500
but you can press it
back down again

1928
01:16:52,500 --> 01:16:54,500
with the Rock 'Em Sock 'Em
Robots! By Marx.

1929
01:16:55,010 --> 01:16:56,010
TOM: So, what can I get ya?

1930
01:16:56,010 --> 01:16:58,510
Ouzo, vodka, Sambuca, Pernod,

1931
01:16:58,510 --> 01:17:02,020
Frangelico, Blue Curacao,
Glenmorangie, B&B, Hennessy,

1932
01:17:02,010 --> 01:17:04,010
Tanqueray,
hundred-year-old brandy?

1933
01:17:04,520 --> 01:17:06,020
RICK: I've never needed
a gun to defend myself.

1934
01:17:06,520 --> 01:17:08,020
Yeah, right.

1935
01:17:08,520 --> 01:17:10,020
You probably pay others
to defend you.

1936
01:17:10,020 --> 01:17:11,530
TOM: No, I use a woman
as a shield.

1937
01:17:13,520 --> 01:17:14,520
What the hell
are you doing?

1938
01:17:14,530 --> 01:17:16,030
CROW: Beer and a shot,
like you said.

1939
01:17:17,530 --> 01:17:19,030
TOM: All right, all right,

1940
01:17:19,030 --> 01:17:21,030
I'll get the smoky
12-year-old scotch.

1941
01:17:21,030 --> 01:17:23,040
Okay.

1942
01:17:26,540 --> 01:17:27,540
What are you doing?

1943
01:17:27,540 --> 01:17:29,540
JOEL: He shot my Jim Beam
pheasant decanter!

1944
01:17:30,040 --> 01:17:31,040
He's gone crazy.

1945
01:17:32,540 --> 01:17:34,040
Look.
What is it with you two?

1946
01:17:34,550 --> 01:17:35,550
Haven't we got enough trouble?

1947
01:17:36,550 --> 01:17:38,050
I don't like anyone bugging me.

1948
01:17:38,050 --> 01:17:39,050
TOM: Yeah.

1949
01:17:39,050 --> 01:17:40,050
[ Knocking on door ]

1950
01:17:40,050 --> 01:17:42,060
TOMMY: Mommy, open the door.
Let me in.

1951
01:17:43,050 --> 01:17:43,550
It's Tommy.

1952
01:17:44,060 --> 01:17:45,560
TOM: I'll get him.
[ Imitates gun cocking ]

1953
01:17:45,560 --> 01:17:47,560
CROW: Tommy, throw open the door
and say "pull".

1954
01:17:48,060 --> 01:17:48,560
[ Crow giggling ]

1955
01:17:49,060 --> 01:17:50,060
[ Tom chuckling ]

1956
01:17:50,560 --> 01:17:52,070
MOLLY: Where did you spring
from?

1957
01:17:52,060 --> 01:17:53,060
JOEL: From your loins, Mommy.

1958
01:17:53,060 --> 01:17:54,060
Didn't I tell you to stay
in your room?

1959
01:17:54,570 --> 01:17:56,570
I went to pick some plants
for all...

1960
01:17:56,570 --> 01:17:58,570
Plants for all your animals,
I suppose, right?

1961
01:17:58,570 --> 01:18:01,070
That's it. Out they're going
to go in the morning.

1962
01:18:01,070 --> 01:18:03,080
Now, get to your room and
don't move till I tell you to.

1963
01:18:03,570 --> 01:18:04,070
TOM: Ooh.

1964
01:18:04,580 --> 01:18:05,580
Wake up, Kathy.

1965
01:18:05,580 --> 01:18:07,580
TOM: I think I got something
to say to you.

1966
01:18:07,580 --> 01:18:08,580
SHARON: I heard a shot.

1967
01:18:08,580 --> 01:18:10,080
Shot?
You must've been dreaming.

1968
01:18:10,080 --> 01:18:12,090
-Wake up.
-What time is it?

1969
01:18:12,080 --> 01:18:14,580
TOM: You know, I'm starting
not to believe this movie.

1970
01:18:14,590 --> 01:18:16,590
I believed it when Alf
went on the killing spree,

1971
01:18:16,590 --> 01:18:18,090
but now... I don't know.

1972
01:18:18,090 --> 01:18:19,590
I don't know. I just hear voices
from downstairs.

1973
01:18:20,090 --> 01:18:22,100
Wow. Those pills
sure are strong.

1974
01:18:22,590 --> 01:18:25,090
I'm going to take a shower
and try to wake myself up.

1975
01:18:25,100 --> 01:18:26,100
-That's a good idea.
-TOM: Say.

1976
01:18:26,100 --> 01:18:27,100
But don't take too long.

1977
01:18:27,600 --> 01:18:28,100
TOM: Oh.

1978
01:18:29,100 --> 01:18:32,610
CROW: Honey, I'm home.
Oh, I'm a little kid.

1979
01:18:35,110 --> 01:18:36,110
JOEL: Nosy?

1980
01:18:36,610 --> 01:18:38,110
TOM: Chirpy?

1981
01:18:38,610 --> 01:18:40,610
CROW: Ratboy? Sondra Locke?

1982
01:18:40,610 --> 01:18:43,120
-TOM: Chief?
-CROW: McCloud?

1983
01:18:43,110 --> 01:18:46,110
JOEL: Now, for my
wonderful experiment

1984
01:18:46,120 --> 01:18:49,120
of joining a duck's body
to a rabbit's head.

1985
01:18:49,620 --> 01:18:51,120
There.

1986
01:18:53,120 --> 01:18:54,120
[ Tom humming ]

1987
01:18:54,130 --> 01:18:57,630
TOM:
I'm all alone in the world

1988
01:18:59,130 --> 01:19:01,640
Hey, the evil one's back.

1989
01:19:01,630 --> 01:19:02,630
-TOMMY: Trumpy.
-TOM: Yay!

1990
01:19:02,630 --> 01:19:04,130
CROW: Hey, it's like that scene
in "Mac and Me"

1991
01:19:04,140 --> 01:19:05,640
when Mac came back to life!

1992
01:19:05,640 --> 01:19:07,140
TOMMY: No, stay there.

1993
01:19:07,640 --> 01:19:09,140
Why did you kill that girl?

1994
01:19:09,640 --> 01:19:12,150
Why did you do that?

1995
01:19:12,640 --> 01:19:14,640
Now I can't be
your friend anymore.

1996
01:19:14,650 --> 01:19:16,150
-TOM: Bad hell beast.
-CROW: Did it for the kicks.

1997
01:19:17,150 --> 01:19:19,150
TOMMY: You're naughty, Trumpy.
Very naughty.

1998
01:19:19,150 --> 01:19:20,650
JOEL: Where have you been,
young man?

1999
01:19:20,650 --> 01:19:21,660
This is not a hotel.

2000
01:19:23,650 --> 01:19:25,150
TOMMY: You wouldn't kill me,
would you?

2001
01:19:26,160 --> 01:19:27,160
[ Tom laughs ]

2002
01:19:29,160 --> 01:19:32,170
Trumpy, was it you?

2003
01:19:32,660 --> 01:19:34,660
TOM: I like you, Tommy.
I'll kill you last.

2004
01:19:34,670 --> 01:19:36,170
TOMMY: Are you saying
there's another one?

2005
01:19:38,170 --> 01:19:41,170
Listen, Trumpy.
Uncle Bill wants to kill you.

2006
01:19:41,670 --> 01:19:43,670
JOEL: My advice...
don't let him.

2007
01:19:48,180 --> 01:19:49,680
JOEL: Looks real bad for you,
man.

2008
01:19:50,180 --> 01:19:51,180
What can we do?

2009
01:19:51,180 --> 01:19:52,690
TOM: Oh, you could put on a play
in the backyard.

2010
01:19:52,680 --> 01:19:54,180
Trumpy could play Cyrano.

2011
01:19:54,690 --> 01:19:57,190
TOMMY: You can't stay here
anymore.

2012
01:19:58,190 --> 01:20:00,690
And I don't want you to go.

2013
01:20:00,690 --> 01:20:03,700
Listen. We'll go together
and hide in the woods.

2014
01:20:04,200 --> 01:20:07,200
No, wait here.
I'll find you a disguise.

2015
01:20:07,700 --> 01:20:09,200
CROW: What do you think he's
going to dress him up as...

2016
01:20:09,200 --> 01:20:10,200
Drew Barrymore?

2017
01:20:10,200 --> 01:20:13,710
-JOEL: Henry Thomas he's not.
-No.

2018
01:20:14,210 --> 01:20:16,710
TOM: Oh, suddenly I feel like
someone should be reading

2019
01:20:16,710 --> 01:20:18,710
a Robert Frost poem.

2020
01:20:18,710 --> 01:20:22,720
"Something there is that doesn't
love a crummy monster film."

2021
01:20:25,220 --> 01:20:28,720
That's from "Mending Monster
Film" by Robert Frost.

2022
01:20:37,730 --> 01:20:39,230
-CROW: Neat.
-TOM: Mm-hm.

2023
01:20:40,730 --> 01:20:41,740
CROW: Mint julep?

2024
01:20:41,730 --> 01:20:44,230
[ Belches ]
TOM: Uh, no thanks. I've had 12.

2025
01:20:46,240 --> 01:20:47,740
JOEL: Sure hope the liquor
holds out.

2026
01:20:48,740 --> 01:20:49,740
TOM: I don't know.

2027
01:20:56,750 --> 01:20:59,250
[ Joel humming ]

2028
01:20:59,250 --> 01:20:59,750
JOEL: I'm in the shower

2029
01:21:00,250 --> 01:21:01,760
Nothing will happen to me

2030
01:21:01,750 --> 01:21:03,250
[ Imitating mother from Psycho ]
CROW: Norman? Norman?

2031
01:21:04,260 --> 01:21:05,760
Important phone call!

2032
01:21:06,260 --> 01:21:07,760
TOM: I wonder if Bobby likes me.

2033
01:21:08,260 --> 01:21:09,760
I like him.

2034
01:21:11,760 --> 01:21:14,260
JOEL: Check it out.
Product placement right there.

2035
01:21:14,270 --> 01:21:15,270
Yep.

2036
01:21:16,270 --> 01:21:17,270
[ Tom chuckling ]

2037
01:21:17,270 --> 01:21:19,270
TOM: "Die Hard 2" this is not.

2038
01:21:20,270 --> 01:21:22,780
CROW: Hmm... Coke, Sprite,
Pepto-Bismol,

2039
01:21:22,770 --> 01:21:25,270
United Airlines,
Steve Guttenberg.

2040
01:21:27,780 --> 01:21:28,780
TOM: Uh-huh.

2041
01:21:29,780 --> 01:21:33,290
There. Now you look like Admiral
Peary playing the Elephant Man.

2042
01:21:34,290 --> 01:21:37,290
TOMMY: Hold on a minute.
I'll go and investigate.

2043
01:21:37,290 --> 01:21:42,300
JOEL: Trumpy felt scarred
by his ugly hillbilly... nose.

2044
01:21:43,290 --> 01:21:45,290
CROW: Looks like a baseball bat
from Alaska.

2045
01:21:46,300 --> 01:21:48,800
TOM: Oh, Velvet Hammer?
Harvey Wallbanger?

2046
01:21:48,800 --> 01:21:51,300
Pink Squirrel? Little hair
of the alien that bit ya?

2047
01:21:51,300 --> 01:21:52,310
[ Tom chuckles ]

2048
01:21:55,310 --> 01:21:56,310
[ Crow hums ]

2049
01:21:56,310 --> 01:21:58,310
CROW: I'm naked and all alone
in the shower.

2050
01:21:58,310 --> 01:22:00,310
I'm totally vulnerable
and somebody could kill me.

2051
01:22:00,310 --> 01:22:01,310
[ Continues to hum ]

2052
01:22:02,310 --> 01:22:03,310
TOM: It's probably likely
at this point in the film.

2053
01:22:03,310 --> 01:22:04,310
CROW: My brain fell out.

2054
01:22:05,820 --> 01:22:08,320
JOEL: Say, I look just like fog.

2055
01:22:08,820 --> 01:22:09,820
TOM: Hmm?

2056
01:22:09,820 --> 01:22:10,820
JOEL: Oh.

2057
01:22:12,320 --> 01:22:15,320
[ Crow imitating squeaking ]

2058
01:22:18,330 --> 01:22:19,830
CROW: You need a protein rinse.

2059
01:22:20,330 --> 01:22:21,330
And you have dandruff.

2060
01:22:23,330 --> 01:22:24,330
TOM: Uh, honey...

2061
01:22:24,340 --> 01:22:25,340
[ Kathy screams ]

2062
01:22:25,340 --> 01:22:27,840
CROW: What? What, what?
What?

2063
01:22:28,840 --> 01:22:30,840
[ Screaming continues ]

2064
01:22:32,340 --> 01:22:33,840
TOM: Wait! Wait, I made you
a special drink.

2065
01:22:33,840 --> 01:22:35,340
Don't forget the coaster!

2066
01:22:36,350 --> 01:22:37,350
SHARON: Rick!

2067
01:22:38,850 --> 01:22:39,850
Brian!

2068
01:22:40,850 --> 01:22:41,860
TOM: Somebody!

2069
01:22:41,850 --> 01:22:42,850
RICK: Kathy!

2070
01:22:44,360 --> 01:22:45,860
[ Kathy screams ]
TOM: Ooh.

2071
01:22:46,360 --> 01:22:47,860
CROW: Don't look at me
without makeup.

2072
01:22:51,860 --> 01:22:53,360
-TOM: Whoa.
-JOEL: Oops.

2073
01:22:54,370 --> 01:22:55,370
RICK: Open the door!

2074
01:22:55,370 --> 01:22:56,870
-CROW: But not with your skull.
-SHARON: Molly!

2075
01:22:56,870 --> 01:22:58,870
-MOLLY: What's happened?
-SHARON: It's Kathy.

2076
01:22:58,870 --> 01:23:00,370
TOM: She's zestfully dead.

2077
01:23:00,870 --> 01:23:01,880
[ Tom chuckling ]

2078
01:23:03,870 --> 01:23:04,870
TOM: Ow.

2079
01:23:05,380 --> 01:23:07,380
MOLLY: Quickly, get her
onto the bed.

2080
01:23:07,880 --> 01:23:09,380
JOEL: Uh, you know,
this might sound crass,

2081
01:23:09,380 --> 01:23:11,380
but we're getting
really good at this.

2082
01:23:11,380 --> 01:23:12,890
CROW: They're going to have
to build an addition

2083
01:23:12,880 --> 01:23:13,880
just to stack the bodies.

2084
01:23:13,880 --> 01:23:14,880
SHARON: What's happening here?

2085
01:23:14,890 --> 01:23:15,890
TOM: How big
is a cord of bodies?

2086
01:23:15,890 --> 01:23:17,390
What was that thing?

2087
01:23:17,390 --> 01:23:17,890
CROW: Depends on how you
stack them.

2088
01:23:18,390 --> 01:23:18,890
BILL: Some kind of weird animal.

2089
01:23:19,890 --> 01:23:20,890
-Where are Brian and Tracy?
-JOEL: What have I done?

2090
01:23:21,390 --> 01:23:22,900
JOEL: What have I done?

2091
01:23:22,890 --> 01:23:23,890
Oh, my goodness.

2092
01:23:26,400 --> 01:23:28,900
TOMMY: Trumpy,
what are you doing here?

2093
01:23:28,900 --> 01:23:30,400
-Go on.
-TOM: Killing people.

2094
01:23:32,400 --> 01:23:33,900
-Tommy?
-JOEL: Can you hear me?

2095
01:23:33,900 --> 01:23:35,900
-Tommy!
-JOEL: Can you feel me near you?

2096
01:23:35,910 --> 01:23:37,910
TOMMY: We can't play now.
Something's happened downstairs.

2097
01:23:37,910 --> 01:23:38,910
You've gotta hide.

2098
01:23:38,910 --> 01:23:40,410
CROW: You're my alibi, kid.

2099
01:23:41,410 --> 01:23:43,420
TOM: They'll kill you.
They'll kill you dead.

2100
01:23:44,420 --> 01:23:47,920
[ Sniffs ]
JOEL: This thing smells musty.

2101
01:23:49,920 --> 01:23:53,430
-MOLLY: Tommy.
-What is it, Mom?

2102
01:23:53,420 --> 01:23:54,920
-Are you all right, son?
-Mm-hm.

2103
01:23:55,430 --> 01:23:56,930
CROW: Well, relatively speaking,
yes.

2104
01:23:56,930 --> 01:23:58,930
Depends on what the norm is.

2105
01:24:00,430 --> 01:24:02,440
RICK: Are you sure we ought
to go after it now, Bill?

2106
01:24:02,430 --> 01:24:04,430
Now's the time to finish
the damn thing off.

2107
01:24:04,440 --> 01:24:05,940
Once and for all.

2108
01:24:05,940 --> 01:24:07,440
It's wounded,
and we can follow its trail.

2109
01:24:07,440 --> 01:24:08,440
Don't go, Rick.

2110
01:24:08,440 --> 01:24:09,940
Isn't it better to wait
till morning?

2111
01:24:09,940 --> 01:24:11,950
I tell you, Molly. Now is
the time to finish it off.

2112
01:24:11,940 --> 01:24:14,440
But, Bill, why don't you leave
it for the rangers?

2113
01:24:14,450 --> 01:24:14,950
Isn't it their...?

2114
01:24:14,950 --> 01:24:15,950
Molly, we can't just sit here

2115
01:24:15,950 --> 01:24:17,950
waiting for it to come back
and kill us all.

2116
01:24:18,950 --> 01:24:20,950
TOM: Yeah, we got plenty
of booze. Let's go ahead.

2117
01:24:20,950 --> 01:24:21,960
BILL: And we gotta do it now.

2118
01:24:21,950 --> 01:24:23,950
It's not a monster.
It wants to be our friend.

2119
01:24:23,950 --> 01:24:25,950
How can you say that
after all that's happened?

2120
01:24:26,460 --> 01:24:27,460
'Cause it's true.

2121
01:24:28,460 --> 01:24:30,460
They all want to be our friends,
but we won't let them.

2122
01:24:30,460 --> 01:24:31,460
That's enough talking...

2123
01:24:31,460 --> 01:24:33,470
JOEL: Oh, that's silly.
Finish your tequila.

2124
01:24:33,460 --> 01:24:34,460
RICK: Don't worry.
We'll be careful.

2125
01:24:34,470 --> 01:24:35,470
Don't go. There's been
enough killing.

2126
01:24:36,470 --> 01:24:37,970
CROW: Stop the madness!

2127
01:24:37,970 --> 01:24:39,470
TOM: Last call, everybody.
Finish them up.

2128
01:24:39,470 --> 01:24:40,470
You coming or not?

2129
01:24:43,970 --> 01:24:46,970
TOM: Ah, we'll take a bottle.
Got a hip flask in the car.

2130
01:24:47,480 --> 01:24:48,980
JOEL: Hey, he's mixing
his leathers now.

2131
01:24:48,980 --> 01:24:50,480
TOM: Eww!

2132
01:24:50,480 --> 01:24:51,480
CROW: Wonder what they wanted?

2133
01:24:51,980 --> 01:24:52,980
Hmm?

2134
01:24:54,490 --> 01:24:55,490
[ Tom humming ]

2135
01:24:55,490 --> 01:24:58,990
MOLLY: Sharon! Tommy! Both
of you, quickly, come over here!

2136
01:24:58,990 --> 01:24:59,990
Get away from it!

2137
01:24:59,990 --> 01:25:00,990
[ Tom chuckling ]
Oh, my God!

2138
01:25:01,490 --> 01:25:03,000
TOMMY: No, Mommy.
Don't shoot him.

2139
01:25:03,490 --> 01:25:03,990
Tommy!

2140
01:25:05,000 --> 01:25:07,500
Trumpy is good.
It wasn't him.

2141
01:25:08,000 --> 01:25:09,500
JOEL: What he's done is good.

2142
01:25:09,500 --> 01:25:10,500
MOLLY: Tommy, get away from it!

2143
01:25:11,000 --> 01:25:12,040
No, Mommy, don't shoot.
Please.

2144
01:25:12,040 --> 01:25:13,540
TOM: Don't make your mother
kill him.

2145
01:25:14,540 --> 01:25:16,040
Tommy, it's going to kill you!

2146
01:25:16,040 --> 01:25:17,540
CROW: I know what you're
thinking, Tommy.

2147
01:25:17,540 --> 01:25:19,550
"Did mom fire six shots
or only five?"

2148
01:25:20,040 --> 01:25:21,040
MOLLY: Tommy!

2149
01:25:22,050 --> 01:25:24,050
[ Drums ]

2150
01:25:29,490 --> 01:25:30,990
JOEL: John Bonham. Moby Dick.

2151
01:25:31,490 --> 01:25:34,990
-MOLLY: Tommy! Tommy, come back!
-TOM: Shane! Come back, Shane!

2152
01:25:34,990 --> 01:25:37,000
Come back! Tommy!

2153
01:25:36,990 --> 01:25:39,490
-CROW: Run, Rusty, run.
-TOM: Run, Eliza, run.

2154
01:25:39,500 --> 01:25:41,770
JOEL: You know, that Trumpy
is one ugly...

2155
01:25:41,770 --> 01:25:42,770
CROW & TOM: Shut yo' mouth!

2156
01:25:42,770 --> 01:25:45,270
JOEL: Hey, I'm only talking
about Trumpy, can you dig it?

2157
01:25:45,770 --> 01:25:47,270
BILL: We have to cross over
to the other side.

2158
01:25:47,270 --> 01:25:48,270
Let's go.

2159
01:25:48,270 --> 01:25:50,280
TOM: Break on through
to the other side, man.

2160
01:25:50,270 --> 01:25:51,270
[ Tom laughs ]

2161
01:25:52,280 --> 01:25:54,780
CROW: Buddy Rich on drums.

2162
01:25:58,280 --> 01:26:01,290
TOM: Backed up
by Bill Kreutzmann.

2163
01:26:05,290 --> 01:26:08,800
MOLLY: Tommy! Tommy!
Where are you?

2164
01:26:09,790 --> 01:26:11,790
TOM: Fortunately, Molly
was a LLRP in 'Nam

2165
01:26:11,800 --> 01:26:14,300
and knows how to track
a boy with a snout-nosed pal.

2166
01:26:14,800 --> 01:26:15,800
BILL: I walked down stream
in the water.

2167
01:26:16,300 --> 01:26:17,300
It's a clever...

2168
01:26:22,310 --> 01:26:23,310
We'll never find him now.

2169
01:26:23,810 --> 01:26:24,810
Tommy!

2170
01:26:27,810 --> 01:26:28,820
We must go faster.

2171
01:26:28,810 --> 01:26:30,310
CROW: Yeah, yeah,
keep your shirt on.

2172
01:26:30,810 --> 01:26:32,310
I'm wearing a big stuffed suit.

2173
01:26:34,320 --> 01:26:35,320
RICK: Not a trace.

2174
01:26:38,820 --> 01:26:39,820
TOM: Who?

2175
01:26:40,320 --> 01:26:41,320
RICK: We'll have to wait
till daylight.

2176
01:26:41,830 --> 01:26:43,330
CROW: Daylight looks
like night anyhow.

2177
01:26:44,330 --> 01:26:45,330
What's it now?

2178
01:26:45,830 --> 01:26:46,830
TOM: Day for night, I think.

2179
01:26:46,830 --> 01:26:48,330
Oh. Thank you, Truffaut.

2180
01:26:48,330 --> 01:26:51,340
JOEL: Well, let's go home.
Our job is done here.

2181
01:26:54,340 --> 01:26:56,340
TOMMY: Someone's coming.
Get down.

2182
01:26:56,340 --> 01:26:57,840
CROW: Splendor in the grass.

2183
01:26:57,840 --> 01:26:59,850
TOM: Grazing in the grass
is a gas.

2184
01:27:00,840 --> 01:27:01,840
JOEL: Can you dig it?

2185
01:27:02,350 --> 01:27:03,350
CROW: High-weed surfin'.

2186
01:27:03,850 --> 01:27:04,350
TOMMY: Ssh.

2187
01:27:05,350 --> 01:27:07,350
TOM: Ssh. Would you...
Would you...

2188
01:27:07,350 --> 01:27:08,860
TOMMY: They mustn't find us.

2189
01:27:10,850 --> 01:27:12,850
[ Tom coughs ]

2190
01:27:15,360 --> 01:27:17,360
-TOM: Vapor action.
-Trumpy.

2191
01:27:23,370 --> 01:27:24,870
Trumpy, where are you hiding?

2192
01:27:24,870 --> 01:27:29,380
[ Whistling theme
from "Lassie" ]

2193
01:27:31,380 --> 01:27:32,380
[ Tom coughing ]

2194
01:27:33,380 --> 01:27:35,380
TOM: Boy, he's going to need
that gas mask.

2195
01:27:40,380 --> 01:27:42,380
CROW: Oh, Trumpy, gross.

2196
01:27:42,390 --> 01:27:44,390
TOM: You stepped
in some Trumpy-dumpy.

2197
01:27:44,890 --> 01:27:46,390
JOEL: You guys, come on.

2198
01:27:46,890 --> 01:27:47,890
[ Gasps ]

2199
01:27:50,890 --> 01:27:51,390
[ Continues to gasp ]

2200
01:27:54,400 --> 01:27:55,400
JOEL: Whoops.

2201
01:27:55,400 --> 01:27:57,900
[ Chuckles ] TOM: I'm gonna
batter fry you, kid.

2202
01:27:57,900 --> 01:27:59,410
CROW: Come on, over the plate,
man.

2203
01:28:01,910 --> 01:28:03,410
Mommy!

2204
01:28:03,410 --> 01:28:04,410
CROW: Come on, rocket it in,
man. Over the plate. Come on.

2205
01:28:04,410 --> 01:28:05,910
-Trumpy!
-TOM: Kid, you were set up.

2206
01:28:05,910 --> 01:28:06,910
TOMMY: Mommy!

2207
01:28:08,910 --> 01:28:09,410
RICK: Sounded like Tommy.

2208
01:28:09,410 --> 01:28:11,410
CROW: No, it wasn't.
It was "Mommy."

2209
01:28:11,420 --> 01:28:15,920
It was an "M" sound. "Mmm,"
like Manhattan, Mimosa.

2210
01:28:15,920 --> 01:28:16,920
MOLLY: Tommy!

2211
01:28:19,420 --> 01:28:20,920
Tommy, where are you?

2212
01:28:21,930 --> 01:28:22,930
JOEL: This is, like,
more intense

2213
01:28:23,430 --> 01:28:25,930
than when Bobby Brady got lost
in the Grand Canyon!

2214
01:28:25,930 --> 01:28:26,930
TOM: Oh, no, wasn't that
in Hawaii?

2215
01:28:26,930 --> 01:28:28,940
JOEL: No, that was where Peter
found that Buddha thing.

2216
01:28:28,930 --> 01:28:30,930
-CROW: Oh, yeah. That was cool.
-TOM: Oh, yeah.

2217
01:28:31,440 --> 01:28:33,440
TOMMY: Don't hurt me.
I'm not like the others.

2218
01:28:33,440 --> 01:28:35,440
[ Tom & Joel mewing ]

2219
01:28:35,440 --> 01:28:35,940
CROW: Ouch.

2220
01:28:36,440 --> 01:28:37,440
[ Tom continues mewing ]

2221
01:28:37,940 --> 01:28:40,450
TOMMY: I'll help you.
I'm not just one of them.

2222
01:28:40,440 --> 01:28:41,440
That's all.

2223
01:28:41,950 --> 01:28:42,950
Let me see.

2224
01:28:42,950 --> 01:28:44,450
CROW: Stay away from that.
It still hurts.

2225
01:28:45,950 --> 01:28:48,960
TOMMY: I'm sorry. Don't worry.

2226
01:28:49,450 --> 01:28:51,450
I'd just like to help you.

2227
01:28:51,460 --> 01:28:53,460
JOEL: I conspire against my own.

2228
01:28:53,460 --> 01:28:54,960
[ Tom mewing ]

2229
01:28:55,460 --> 01:28:56,460
RICK: No.

2230
01:28:56,960 --> 01:28:58,970
I'll blast one.
You take the other.

2231
01:28:59,460 --> 01:29:01,460
No, please don't hurt them.

2232
01:29:02,970 --> 01:29:04,470
Get out of the way, Tommy.

2233
01:29:04,470 --> 01:29:05,970
Get out of the way!

2234
01:29:05,970 --> 01:29:07,970
No, don't hurt them, please.

2235
01:29:07,970 --> 01:29:09,980
TOM: Move it, kid. I'll have
a banana daiquiri, please.

2236
01:29:09,970 --> 01:29:11,470
TOMMY: Run, Trumpy. Run!

2237
01:29:12,480 --> 01:29:12,980
No, Bill!

2238
01:29:14,480 --> 01:29:14,980
[ Screams ]

2239
01:29:15,480 --> 01:29:17,980
TOM: Long Island iced tea.

2240
01:29:18,980 --> 01:29:20,480
[ Creature screams ]

2241
01:29:20,480 --> 01:29:22,980
JOEL: Hey, looks like he came
from the Dumbo planet.

2242
01:29:23,490 --> 01:29:25,990
CROW: Time to take the mask off
and see who it is.

2243
01:29:25,990 --> 01:29:26,990
Do you folks at home know?

2244
01:29:30,990 --> 01:29:31,990
MOLLY: Tommy!

2245
01:29:33,500 --> 01:29:35,000
CROW: Oh, my ankle.
It's all bendy-wendy.

2246
01:29:37,000 --> 01:29:38,500
SHARON: Molly, we'll find him.

2247
01:29:38,500 --> 01:29:41,010
TOM: We may find him dead,
but we will find him.

2248
01:29:42,510 --> 01:29:45,510
JOEL: Boy, I hope he left
the keys to the liquor cabinet.

2249
01:29:45,510 --> 01:29:46,510
TOM: Poor sap.

2250
01:29:49,010 --> 01:29:51,010
CROW: Oh, self-bury monster.

2251
01:29:51,010 --> 01:29:52,010
Explain that.

2252
01:29:54,520 --> 01:29:55,020
TOM: Soft beach.

2253
01:29:57,520 --> 01:29:58,520
SHARON: Oh.

2254
01:30:00,520 --> 01:30:03,520
JOEL: And he died as he lived,
with his mouth wide open.

2255
01:30:04,530 --> 01:30:05,530
MOLLY: Where's Tommy?

2256
01:30:05,530 --> 01:30:06,530
He went that way.

2257
01:30:06,530 --> 01:30:08,030
Wait, Molly! Come on.

2258
01:30:10,030 --> 01:30:11,530
Trumpy, I'm sorry.

2259
01:30:12,040 --> 01:30:13,040
Tommy!

2260
01:30:14,540 --> 01:30:16,040
Tommy, answer me, please!

2261
01:30:16,040 --> 01:30:18,040
CROW: State it in the form
of a question.

2262
01:30:18,040 --> 01:30:21,050
-Tommy! Where are you?
-TOM: Come to the mirror, boy!

2263
01:30:23,550 --> 01:30:24,550
TOM: Mm-hm.

2264
01:30:24,550 --> 01:30:26,550
TOMMY: It's just no good.
No, Trumpy.

2265
01:30:26,550 --> 01:30:28,550
They'll never let us stay
together.

2266
01:30:29,550 --> 01:30:31,050
You frighten them.
You understand?

2267
01:30:31,050 --> 01:30:32,050
TOM: For obvious reasons.

2268
01:30:32,060 --> 01:30:34,060
I'll never forget you, Trumpy.

2269
01:30:34,060 --> 01:30:36,060
TOM: The way you callously
knocked off 15 people.

2270
01:30:36,060 --> 01:30:39,570
I'll never forget that.
Don't ever change, Trumpy.

2271
01:30:42,070 --> 01:30:43,070
Aww.

2272
01:30:43,070 --> 01:30:44,570
JOEL: A tender moment.

2273
01:30:45,070 --> 01:30:46,070
[ Weeping ]

2274
01:30:47,070 --> 01:30:49,080
TOMMY: Now, please go
and don't come back.

2275
01:30:49,570 --> 01:30:51,070
Do you understand?

2276
01:30:51,580 --> 01:30:53,080
Don't ever come back.

2277
01:30:53,580 --> 01:30:55,580
Tommy, where are you?

2278
01:30:56,580 --> 01:30:58,080
Go away, Trumpy.

2279
01:30:58,080 --> 01:30:59,590
I hate you. Go away.

2280
01:30:59,580 --> 01:31:01,580
JOEL: Oh, boy, that kid's
really having mood swings.

2281
01:31:01,590 --> 01:31:03,590
-We're not friends anymore.
-JOEL: That's not good.

2282
01:31:03,590 --> 01:31:04,590
TOMMY: Go away.

2283
01:31:05,590 --> 01:31:07,090
All right, Trumpy.
[ Tom mewing ]

2284
01:31:07,590 --> 01:31:09,600
I'll go, then.

2285
01:31:09,590 --> 01:31:11,590
I'm over here, Mommy.

2286
01:31:11,600 --> 01:31:14,100
CROW: Talkin' to Billy Barty.

2287
01:31:15,100 --> 01:31:17,100
[ Tom mewing ]

2288
01:31:18,600 --> 01:31:21,110
Mommy, I'm here!

2289
01:31:22,110 --> 01:31:22,610
TOM: Uh-huh.

2290
01:31:23,110 --> 01:31:25,110
RICK: Molly, he's here.

2291
01:31:25,110 --> 01:31:26,610
JOEL: No, he's over there.

2292
01:31:27,110 --> 01:31:28,110
MOLLY: Tommy!

2293
01:31:30,610 --> 01:31:31,610
Mom!

2294
01:31:31,620 --> 01:31:33,120
TOM: Sorry, boy,
your uncle's dead,

2295
01:31:33,620 --> 01:31:35,120
but if there's a God
and he tends bar,

2296
01:31:35,120 --> 01:31:37,120
your uncle's bellying up
right about now.

2297
01:31:37,120 --> 01:31:38,120
RICK: Yes, Tommy,
all the monsters are dead.

2298
01:31:38,120 --> 01:31:40,130
Isn't that right?

2299
01:31:40,120 --> 01:31:41,620
[ Synth music plays ]

2300
01:31:41,630 --> 01:31:43,130
TOM:
It's been seven

2301
01:31:43,130 --> 01:31:45,130
Oh, never mind.

2302
01:31:48,130 --> 01:31:51,140
CROW: Hey, don't leave me here.
I was raised by a child.

2303
01:31:51,130 --> 01:31:53,130
I can't survive
in the wilderness.

2304
01:31:54,140 --> 01:31:55,140
[ Tom mewing ]

2305
01:31:55,140 --> 01:31:57,640
I'll... just... wait here, then.

2306
01:31:57,640 --> 01:32:00,650
[ Mewing continues ]

2307
01:32:06,150 --> 01:32:07,150
TOM: So...

2308
01:32:07,150 --> 01:32:08,150
[ Sighs ]

2309
01:32:09,650 --> 01:32:11,650
CROW: Hmm.

2310
01:32:12,660 --> 01:32:13,160
TOM: Mm-hm.

2311
01:32:13,660 --> 01:32:18,160
JOEL:
I've laughed with monsters

2312
01:32:18,160 --> 01:32:22,170
JOEL & TOM:
I've cried with monsters

2313
01:32:22,670 --> 01:32:27,170
JOEL & TOM: I'll die
with monsters from hell

2314
01:32:27,170 --> 01:32:29,180
CROW: I'm getting out of here.
This place sucks.

2315
01:32:29,170 --> 01:32:30,170
[ Tom chuckles ]

2316
01:32:31,170 --> 01:32:32,170
CROW: Going back to my planet.

2317
01:32:33,180 --> 01:32:36,180
TOM: Hmm, Marine?

2318
01:32:36,180 --> 01:32:37,680
[ Chuckling ]
Send in the marines.

2319
01:32:37,680 --> 01:32:38,180
CROW: Hey.

2320
01:32:41,180 --> 01:32:43,180
JOEL: Ah, isn't that
Martin Sheen's son?

2321
01:32:43,690 --> 01:32:44,690
CROW: Hey, who isn't?

2322
01:32:44,690 --> 01:32:46,690
-JOEL: Yeah, got a point there.
-TOM: Yep.

2323
01:32:49,690 --> 01:32:52,190
TOM: Ooh, that's a good
Italian lunch wine.

2324
01:32:52,200 --> 01:32:53,200
Very light.

2325
01:32:53,200 --> 01:32:55,200
Smooth palate,
a nice woody finish.

2326
01:32:57,700 --> 01:32:59,710
JOEL: Hey, Martin and Lewis
were in this movie.

2327
01:32:59,700 --> 01:33:00,700
CROW: Come on, Jerry,

2328
01:33:01,200 --> 01:33:03,200
we've got the rest
of the credits to get through.

2329
01:33:03,210 --> 01:33:03,710
JOEL: Wow, Dean.

2330
01:33:03,710 --> 01:33:05,210
CROW: Aw, quit horsing around,
boy.

2331
01:33:05,210 --> 01:33:06,210
[ Tom sniffs ]

2332
01:33:06,210 --> 01:33:09,220
TOM: Ah, the fresh smell
of Emanuel Pine.

2333
01:33:10,210 --> 01:33:11,710
CROW: Long needle.

2334
01:33:14,220 --> 01:33:16,720
JOEL: I say both of those guys
were in the Knights of Columbus.

2335
01:33:16,720 --> 01:33:19,230
TOM: I think their Two Guys of
the Rotten Union is what it is.

2336
01:33:19,720 --> 01:33:21,720
CROW: Well, hmm.

2337
01:33:23,730 --> 01:33:26,730
TOM: Oh, I thought
I smelled basil.

2338
01:33:26,730 --> 01:33:27,730
Basil!

2339
01:33:28,230 --> 01:33:29,740
CROW: Yes, dear.
I'm doing it, dear.

2340
01:33:29,730 --> 01:33:31,230
How can I do it if you keep
calling me?

2341
01:33:31,230 --> 01:33:32,230
CROW: Great cow!

2342
01:33:32,240 --> 01:33:33,240
JOEL: Come on,
let's get out of here.

2343
01:33:33,740 --> 01:33:34,740
CROW: Oh, thank you.

2344
01:33:34,740 --> 01:33:35,740
TOM: Chase me.

2345
01:33:35,740 --> 01:33:37,240
CROW: Okay, ha ha ha.

2346
01:33:50,590 --> 01:33:51,390
Well, guys,

2347
01:33:51,890 --> 01:33:54,390
looks like it's time
to pack it all in again.

2348
01:33:54,890 --> 01:33:57,900
Yeah, we are the stuff
dreams are made of.

2349
01:33:57,890 --> 01:33:59,890
TOM: Oh, that's beautiful, Crow.

2350
01:33:59,900 --> 01:34:01,900
-Shakespeare?
-Uh, no, Burma-Shave.

2351
01:34:01,900 --> 01:34:02,900
Oh, well, Iike... Huh?

2352
01:34:02,900 --> 01:34:06,410
You know, guys, it always
hurts to close it all up...

2353
01:34:06,400 --> 01:34:08,400
-Yeah.
-...strike the set...

2354
01:34:08,410 --> 01:34:10,410
-Oww!
-...wipe off the grease paint...

2355
01:34:10,910 --> 01:34:13,910
Uh, napkin up
the blood and entrails

2356
01:34:13,910 --> 01:34:15,410
and move on to another town.

2357
01:34:15,910 --> 01:34:17,910
Uh-oh, I smell a song.

2358
01:34:17,910 --> 01:34:18,910
Mm-hm.

2359
01:34:19,420 --> 01:34:23,420
Tell me, where does
all the magic go

2360
01:34:25,420 --> 01:34:30,930
When the curtain falls
to end the show?

2361
01:34:30,930 --> 01:34:34,430
Do the clowns always cry

2362
01:34:34,930 --> 01:34:40,440
When they pack up
the paper sky?

2363
01:34:40,940 --> 01:34:45,440
When the champagne
is being poured

2364
01:34:46,440 --> 01:34:51,440
And the lock is on the old
stage door?

2365
01:34:52,950 --> 01:34:57,960
Will there still be a clown
in the sky

2366
01:34:58,460 --> 01:35:01,460
For me?

2367
01:35:01,460 --> 01:35:02,960
[ Sobbing ]

2368
01:35:03,960 --> 01:35:04,960
No.

2369
01:35:04,960 --> 01:35:06,970
Don't worry, buddy. There'll be
other experiments.

2370
01:35:06,960 --> 01:35:08,960
You really think so, mister?

2371
01:35:08,970 --> 01:35:10,470
Yeah, take a verse.
It'll cheer you up.

2372
01:35:10,470 --> 01:35:11,470
Okay.

2373
01:35:12,470 --> 01:35:16,480
When the harlequin
is on the bed

2374
01:35:16,970 --> 01:35:20,970
And the whisky haze
surrounds his head

2375
01:35:21,480 --> 01:35:23,480
William Holden's
coming over

2376
01:35:23,480 --> 01:35:25,480
-Tom Servo...
-And he's got a fifth of...

2377
01:35:25,480 --> 01:35:28,490
if you don't stop doing
your Anthony Newley,

2378
01:35:28,490 --> 01:35:30,490
I'm going to throw you
against the wall.

2379
01:35:30,490 --> 01:35:31,490
He'll do it, too.

2380
01:35:31,490 --> 01:35:35,490
Will there still be a clown
in the sky?

2381
01:35:35,490 --> 01:35:36,500
Help us out, Crow.

2382
01:35:36,990 --> 01:35:41,490
Still be a clown
in the sky?

2383
01:35:41,500 --> 01:35:42,500
Take it home, Joel.

2384
01:35:42,500 --> 01:35:47,510
Tell me, where is
that clown in the sky

2385
01:35:48,000 --> 01:35:51,000
For... me?

2386
01:35:51,010 --> 01:35:51,510
[ Sobbing ]
Oh!

2387
01:35:52,010 --> 01:35:53,010
I love you, Tom Servo.

2388
01:35:53,010 --> 01:35:55,010
-I love you, Joel.
-I love you, Crow.

2389
01:35:55,010 --> 01:35:56,520
You're not my real father.

2390
01:35:56,510 --> 01:35:57,510
What do you think, sirs?

2391
01:35:59,020 --> 01:36:00,520
It stinks.

2392
01:37:06,380 --> 01:37:07,380
Well?

2393
01:37:08,390 --> 01:37:09,890
It stinks.

